  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(50\\,\\text{km})^{2} \\\\  & =50\\,\\text{km}\\times 50\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =(50\\times 50)\\times (\\text{km}\\times \\text{km}) \\\\  & =2\\,500\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
